{
  "requirement": "Select a Bedrock model or inference profile with `model`. The optional region, AWS profile, and explicit credentials configure its client. `options` carries inference settings.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct BedrockConfig {\n    pub model: String,\n    pub aws_profile: Option<String>,\n    pub region: Option<String>,\n    pub credentials: Option<BedrockCredentials>,\n    pub options: BTreeMap<String, OptionValue>,\n}\n\nimpl BedrockConfig {\n    pub fn new(model: String) -> Self;\n    pub fn aws_profile(self, aws_profile: String) -> Self;\n    pub fn region(self, region: String) -> Self;\n    pub fn credentials(self, credentials: BedrockCredentials) -> Self;\n    pub fn option(self, key: String, value: OptionValue) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for BedrockConfig;\nimpl Debug for BedrockConfig;\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for BedrockConfig;\nimpl PartialEq for BedrockConfig;\nimpl Serialize for BedrockConfig;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.BedrockConfig`.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that cover them**\n- **Constructor.** `new(model)` sets only `model`. `config.rs#mod[tests]/fn[backend_builders_set_only_the_requested_fields]` asserts that `BedrockConfig::new(\"bedrock-model\")` serializes to exactly `{\"model\":\"bedrock-model\"}`. It also asserts that this equals the value deserialized from the minimal JSON, so the optional fields default to absent.\n- **Builders.** `aws_profile`, `region`, `credentials` and `option` each set their own field. The same test chains all four and asserts the full serialized JSON: `aws_profile`, `region`, nested `credentials` including `session_token`, and `options`.\n- **Option override.** The test inserts `a=1` and `b=true`, then `a=2`. It asserts `options` is `{\"a\":2,\"b\":true}`, so a repeated key replaces the earlier value and the other key is kept.\n- **Serialize and Deserialize.** `config.rs#mod[tests]/fn[all_backends_preserve_nested_settings_and_credentials]` deserializes a full Bedrock configuration (all fields, nested and array options, session token) and asserts it re-serializes to the identical JSON. It also round-trips through a JSON string and asserts equality. This exercises `Deserialize`, `Serialize` and `PartialEq` for `BedrockConfig`, reached through `AgentConfig::Bedrock`.\n- **Derived trait implementations (`Clone`, `Debug`, `PartialEq`, `Serialize`, `Deserialize`), `#[non_exhaustive]`, the struct fields and the method signatures.** `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` is marked `{test}` for `requirements.sdk.public_api`. It runs rustdoc and compares each declaration, field and method signature, and the trait-implementation list, against the book. The helpers reached from it, `check_declaration` and `trait_impls`, assert the expected and documented trait implementations are equal. A missing `Clone` or `Debug` impl would therefore fail this test.\n\n**Gaps**\nI found no unexercised obligation and no wrong expected result. `Clone` and `Debug` have no behavioral tests, but they are derived, have no conditional logic of their own, and their presence is checked by the public API test.",
